  "tempo": 1.12,
  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "That tiny hole in your airplane window is supposed to be there.",
      "start": 0.041,
      "end": 3.078
    },
    {
      "text": "Passenger windows use multiple layers, and that little breather hole sits in one of",
      "start": 3.422,
      "end": 7.833
    },
    {
      "text": "the inner panes.",
      "start": 7.834,
      "end": 8.655
    },
    {
      "text": "It helps manage the pressure between the layers, so the outer structural pane takes",
      "start": 8.962,
      "end": 13.056
    },
    {
      "text": "most of the pressure difference while you're flying at altitude.",
      "start": 13.056,
      "end": 15.753
    },
    {
      "text": "It also helps moisture escape from between the panes.",
      "start": 16.052,
      "end": 18.571
    },
    {
      "text": "So no, your airplane window does not have a manufacturing defect.",
      "start": 18.924,
      "end": 22.317
    },
    {
      "text": "That suspicious little hole is actually part of the reason the window works in the",
      "start": 22.615,
      "end": 26.17
    },
    {
      "text": "1st place.",
      "start": 26.17,
      "end": 26.67
    }
  ],
